{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/932934-lunar-castes-have-always-been-a-bit-different","id":932934,"title":"Lunar Castes have always been a bit different","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-17T09:26:26-07:00","id":932934,"title":"Lunar Castes have always been a bit different","content":"Avoiding a potential derail in Irked's Lunar homebrew thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maudova</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e?p=930697#post930697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are we still stuck with the idea that there are 3 castes? We should have all 5 castes so that Lunars have variability and can focus on areas players want. I think the idea of &quot;breaking&quot; their exaltation a has other more interesting possible avenues.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I have to say at the start won't really engage with what you're saying, but here it is:<br /> <br /> &quot;Lunar Castes have never really been about <i>what </i>you are supposed to do, but rather <i>how </i>you go about doing it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Dawn Castes tend to be the most physical of the Solar Exalted, but there is still a significant social and mental aspect to their role, whether that be intimidating opponents, inspiring soldiers, implementing training regimens and battlefield strategies, or analyzing and responding to the martial techniques and flaws of others. A Dawn can choose <i>how </i>she goes about being a Dawn in what Caste and out-of-Caste Abilities she favors and invests, but she's still fulfilling a role regardless of her specific methods.<br /> <br /> While the Full Moon Caste finds their physical prowess an easy match to physical violence, the social and mental prowess of the Changing Moon and No Moon Caste have their uses in battle. Like Dawns, Changing Moons intimidate opponents and inspire followers, but they also have a somewhat more natural time employing feints and misdirection, and their ability to train followers more naturally encompasses animals (as Survival is not a Dawn Caste Ability). Like Dawns (for whom Awareness <i>is </i>a Caste Ability), No Moons are capable of responding with great sharpness and speed to the actions of their enemies, analyzing their tactics and flaws, and devising clever strategies to achieve victory.<br /> <br /> Caste-specific Role Bonuses for Lunar players to earn Solar Experience wouldn't be about WHAT they did, but more HOW they did something.<br /> <br /> &quot;Did the Full Moon discover a physical solution to what seemed like a firmly social or mental problem? Did he perform a physical feat that put even his Exalted might to the test?&quot; That sort of thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not convinced that Caste-derived &quot;roles&quot; would enhance or fit the Lunar experience, especially given the Lunar ability to BREAK their Castes.<br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun chose a Dawn because he felt that the mortal had the right attitude to take and use the Sun's martial power to change the world. Mars chooses heroes she feels will best facilitate her vision of the conflicts that she wants to happen or prevent in Creation. These choices are very firmly tied to roles that these heroes are intended to play, whether alone or with others. These roles are immutable realities of the Exalted Souls granted to them.<br /> <br /> But the Moon Goddess chooses those heroes who valued their freedom more than life itself, to the point where she actually Exalted a woman for an elaborate act of suicide (throwing herself to the sharks). She rewards this thirst for freedom with the power to attain that freedom and survive.<br /> <br /> This seems very purposeless, leaving her Chosen to find their own direction. In the Primordial War, this direction was to cooperate with the other Exalted in earning humanity's freedom to achieve prosperity and dominion over Creation without needing to fear the creators of the world and their favored species. In the Second Age, this direction is to wage war against the Scarlet Dynasty for the freedom to exist.<br /> <br /> Matching this lack of direction, Luna's Exalted Souls are inherently mutable in a way completely unique to the Exalted Host. A Dawn is a Dawn, a Chosen of Journeys is forever an Exalt of Mercury, no Alchemical can change his primary Magical Material any more than a Terrestrial can change his primary Element.<br /> <br /> I don't get the sense that Luna cares WHAT her Chosen do with their freedom. Would she really be giving them freedom if she immediately burdened them with expectations for what they ought to be doing with themselves? Or would she be giving them more freedom by gifting them with Castes that emphasis their personal talents, and thereby offer them more power for attaining their freedom in the ways that matter most to them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T09:39:16-07:00","id":932936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/932934-lunar-castes-have-always-been-a-bit-different#post932934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Caste-specific Role Bonuses for Lunar players to earn Solar Experience wouldn't be about WHAT they did, but more HOW they did something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will point out that the Night Caste role bonuses are entirely about how it is done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T10:45:17-07:00","id":932962,"title":"","content":"Only problem I've ever really seen with 3 Castes is that if it's a game for an ideal of 5 players, (as it seems to be for all the other splats?), then you have to decide which Castes to double up on.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit leery about the specific example of only giving a bonus to Lunars for using their capabilities in a counter intuitive way (&quot;Solved a mental problem through a social route&quot; etc.) since I think that's both a bit too much in need of interpretation and I think they should be rewarded for doing specific things than doing counter intuitive things only. Otherwise, I think, yes, and role bonus needs to be comparable to the breadth of the caste and its focus (which could be along the lines physical / social / mental?).<br /> <br /> I'm also not so keen on the idea of Luna as a god who is agnostic of what her chosen do in the world, if we're going with gods who care about that at all. IDK why. Just the idea that Sol is the only god / Incarna who cares about what his Chosen are doing in the sense of giving them a mission or purpose understandable to humanity (Sidereals don't, really, in the sense that Fate is a bit of black box) sort of has a bad taste to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T20:15:39-07:00","id":934870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/932934-lunar-castes-have-always-been-a-bit-different#post932934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Avoiding a potential derail in Irked's Lunar homebrew thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoops wasn't intentional. My thought was more on the lines of the limit inherent in selecting 3 castes with 3 Caste attributes, with just three defined rolls. I think it's just inherently limiting to players imagination. During second edition we saw a lot of people poo pooing lunars due to this. It drew in people who loved the idea of shapshifting regardless of mechanical backing vs a cool theme backed by solid mechanics. I've played 2 lunars and both times it was underwhelming due to the inherent limit of basing charms off of attributes with such a limited scope. It was difficult to be a brilliant full moon tactician mechanically. It all boils down to concept should not be limited by mechanic. <br /> <br /> P.S. I am totally using this homebrew for my NPCs until the splat comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T07:21:16-07:00","id":935046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/932934-lunar-castes-have-always-been-a-bit-different?p=932936#post932936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will point out that the Night Caste role bonuses are entirely about how it is done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, all 5 Solar Caste roles are about &quot;how it's done&quot;. Fighting, Inspiring, Thinking, Sneaking, and Negotiating. (Very broad generalizations, I know)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T08:10:48-07:00","id":935076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/932934-lunar-castes-have-always-been-a-bit-different?p=935046#post935046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Truth be told, all 5 Solar Caste roles are about &quot;how it's done&quot;. Fighting, Inspiring, Thinking, Sneaking, and Negotiating. (Very broad generalizations, I know)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes...<br /> <br /> It can be said that they are about how it's done. But it's also about their Role.. More so about the role given then how they do it.<br /> <br /> Consider, A Dawn combat trainer: Primary Focus is on mental aspects of conflict rather then the actual fighting, Confidence, Skill, Analysis and Tactical choice. The &quot;Role&quot; Is for Leading people in conflict and being a General, being Skilled in combat. Although they are more focused on the &quot;How&quot; they are still at the very least capable of fighting Droves of lesser opponents with some ability. That is what Being a Dawn means... You &quot;Fight back the Darkness that takes the land during the Night&quot;<br /> Their Role is Focused on &quot;Fighting&quot; but they are better at &quot;Thinking&quot; and possibly &quot;Inspiring&quot;<br /> <br /> Not negating what you said... but hoping to give a different perception of what that means... Atleast to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T09:58:45-07:00","id":935108,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think RickmanUK is right. A Dawn has something to do with fighting, but might do it himself, inspire others to do it as a general, work out the best way to do it as a strategist, etc.<br /> A Full Moon will do things (generally, castes aren't too limiting) in a physical way. Fight physically, impress people physically, solve puzzles physically, etc.<br /> <br /> But it's probably not helpful to be too specific or limiting.<br /> <br /> Anyway, to get back to the OP (or rather what he's quoting) I see no problem with the 3 Lunar castes, and think having 5 castes would only confuse matters. The 3 Lunar castes are nice and simple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T11:08:09-07:00","id":935142,"title":"","content":"So StG was quoting my response to another posted stating they wanted to get away from one of the castes being the sorcerers amongst the lunars. I agree with the original poster that tagging any one caste with sorcerers anima powers does inherently limit them. In that sense that if they chose to play that caste for whatever reason and they are not a sorcerer that anima power is a useless ability. It shoe horns that caste into being less functionally efficient for the character played or play someone that is initiated. <br /> <br /> My suggestion was based on the idea that if you have 3 and the caste you wanted to play isn't a sorcerer then you only have 2 viable options. Right. So essentially the splat is reduced to two castes at that point. If the character you wanted to play was cerebral then you are stuck with a a physical build trying to be smart of a social build trying to outwit people. Which sure they can be played, however they are not exactly comfortable places to play from (people accepting the challenge aside). Forcing one of 3 castes to integrate sorcery as one for their defining characteristics (as lunar caste tattoos do) is not well thought out. Sure you could replace that anima power with something else non-sorcery based as the person I was reply to said but, that leaves lunar sorcerers in the lurch and without comparable anima effects to support it (Lunar sorcerers were supposed to be an important thing). <br /> <br /> Let compare solars to lunars again. A solar gets 10 abilities. You can make any kind of viable character idea you want with 10 favored/caste abilities. However having all of one stat block plus one doesn't allow you to make a mechanically viable character that comfortably fits within a broad range of roles. Yes sure lunars have a specific set of roles to play as per theme. They don't have to be limited by their core mechanics in a way that limits the characters you can build for them. I've played 2 lunar characters and several solars. It was MUCH easier and more enjoyable to make a character with the solar mechanics than it was to use a lunars. <br /> <br /> Keeping the limitation of 3 castes is honestly a weak reliance on that mechanics having three attribute blocks to correlate castes too. Dropping in 5 castes with a variety of caste attributes in 3rd edition makes just as much sense as how they opened caste and favored abilities up for solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T15:30:10-07:00","id":935301,"title":"","content":"I think the point of having the castes be to set in there ways is a fair problem but you could have something like what they did with solars. Have each caste have Caste Attributes more broad then there 2nd edition set and only able to choose three caste and one favored:<br /> <br /> Full moon: Str, Dex, Stamina, Cha and Wits. They all are important for combat but open up options.<br /> <br /> Changing moon: Stamina, Cha, Man, Appearance and Perception. Perception helps you read something and stamania will help you maintain the physical requirments to dance for hours or sing for a long time Ect.. (Its loose ill admit)<br /> <br /> No moon: Str, Man, Perception, Int and Wits.<br /> <br /> If a supernal Attribute comes up this allows each caste to have its attribute no one else gets:<br /> Full moon: Dex (Since its the most important combat Attribute it protections there top dog in physical combat)<br /> Changing moon: Appearance since it tends to have an effect on social combat in all its forms whether your using manipulation or cha.<br /> No moon: Int since its probably going to be the sorcery thing and seems like the shamans would be the best at anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> This just makes it easy to have Niche protection if one includes some version of supernal attribute into lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8767-rattleingpython","name":"rattleingpython","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T08:40:54-07:00","id":935623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maudova</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/932934-lunar-castes-have-always-been-a-bit-different?p=935142#post935142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So StG was quoting my response to another posted stating they wanted to get away from one of the castes being the sorcerers amongst the lunars. I agree with the original poster that tagging any one caste with sorcerers anima powers does inherently limit them. In that sense that if they chose to play that caste for whatever reason and they are not a sorcerer that anima power is a useless ability. It shoe horns that caste into being less functionally efficient for the character played or play someone that is initiated.<br /> <br /> My suggestion was based on the idea that if you have 3 and the caste you wanted to play isn't a sorcerer then you only have 2 viable options. Right. So essentially the splat is reduced to two castes at that point. If the character you wanted to play was cerebral then you are stuck with a a physical build trying to be smart of a social build trying to outwit people. Which sure they can be played, however they are not exactly comfortable places to play from (people accepting the challenge aside). Forcing one of 3 castes to integrate sorcery as one for their defining characteristics (as lunar caste tattoos do) is not well thought out. Sure you could replace that anima power with something else non-sorcery based as the person I was reply to said but, that leaves lunar sorcerers in the lurch and without comparable anima effects to support it (Lunar sorcerers were supposed to be an important thing).<br /> <br /> Let compare solars to lunars again. A solar gets 10 abilities. You can make any kind of viable character idea you want with 10 favored/caste abilities. However having all of one stat block plus one doesn't allow you to make a mechanically viable character that comfortably fits within a broad range of roles. Yes sure lunars have a specific set of roles to play as per theme. They don't have to be limited by their core mechanics in a way that limits the characters you can build for them. I've played 2 lunar characters and several solars. It was MUCH easier and more enjoyable to make a character with the solar mechanics than it was to use a lunars.<br /> <br /> Keeping the limitation of 3 castes is honestly a weak reliance on that mechanics having three attribute blocks to correlate castes too. Dropping in 5 castes with a variety of caste attributes in 3rd edition makes just as much sense as how they opened caste and favored abilities up for solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, the answer to No Moons being sorcerers all the time, is to let them not be sorcerers. Give them anima powers that are not just about sorcery. And better charms (the Lunar mental charms were crap).<br /> <br /> As to the Caste Attributes being restrictive, well yes, but that's because of the numbers of attributes for the castes compared to Solar castes' abilities. Solars got 5 caste abilites and 5 favoured abilities. Lunars got 3 caste attributes and 1 favoured attribute. I'd suggest giving them another favoured attribute to make them more flexible, rather than sticking in 2 other castes that didn't have much to them.<br /> We actually have always run what the guy who wrote the Lunar charmset, but not the char gen rules, suggested: give Lunars their choice of 2 caste attributes, and also 2 favoured attributes. It works well.<br /> And with the 3e idea that you choose Favoured Attributes out of a list, it seems easy enough to say &quot;No Moons choose 2 caste attributes out of Perception, Intelligence and Wits, and then 2 favoured attributes&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Full moon: Str, Dex, Stamina, Cha and Wits. They all are important for combat but open up options. </div> </div> </div>I'd give Full Moons Appearance and Perception, as they seem more appropriate for a character with incredible physique (and sensitive eyes, ears, etc).<br /> <br /> I wouldn't worry about Supernal though: I think the intention is for non-Solars not to have Supernal, but rather other things that similarly unlock charms, but in a different way. Rising above their limits is the Solar &quot;thing&quot;. One suggestion was for Lunars to find it easier to buy charms connected to their spirit shape, but that was suggested a long time ago, so who knows what the Devs are thinking now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T09:02:54-07:00","id":935632,"title":"","content":"Yeah I'm on the camp that supernal is going to be Solaroid(Solars, Infernals, Abyssals) only. Other splats are going to get something different, that might or might not unlock higher essence charms and might not even allow to pick essence 5 at creation, might stop at essence 2 or 3, since they usually all get a special power associated with their types of exalt.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T10:48:26-07:00","id":935679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/932934-lunar-castes-have-always-been-a-bit-different?p=935623#post935623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, the answer to No Moons being sorcerers all the time, is to let them not be sorcerers. Give them anima powers that are not just about sorcery. And better charms (the Lunar mental charms were crap).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this here, for sure. A lot of Lunar charms I didn't really feel were at the celestial level. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/932934-lunar-castes-have-always-been-a-bit-different?p=935623#post935623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the Caste Attributes being restrictive, well yes, but that's because of the numbers of attributes for the castes compared to Solar castes' abilities. Solars got 5 caste abilities[sic] and 5 favored[sic] abilities. Lunars got 3 caste attributes and 1 favored[sic] attribute. I'd suggest giving them another favoured attribute to make them more flexible, rather than sticking in 2 other castes that didn't have much to them.<br /> We actually have always run what the guy who wrote the Lunar charmset, but not the char gen rules, suggested: give Lunars their choice of 2 caste attributes, and also 2 favored[sic] attributes. It works well.<br /> And with the 3e idea that you choose Favoured Attributes out of a list, it seems easy enough to say &quot;No Moons choose 2 caste attributes out of Perception, Intelligence and Wits, and then 2 favoured attributes&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what would rock? Anima powers based on their caste attributes, keeping with their mercurial natures. That would allow lunars to have a larger selection of caste abilities, another thing I think they lacked (a minor point really), that would be covered by a group of exalted with 5 castes. I would suggest all of the castes have 1 primary caste power that does not change, and then get one anima power per caste attribute. Specifically not their favored attributes. This would allow them to keep the standard 3 anima abilities of the other exalt types. It would also give them that unique flavor as indaviduals as they are not all the same, which seems in theme for them. <br /> <br /> As for which attributes that should be up for grabs as caste or favored I don't know if I would go with the tranditional 3 provided in 2nd ed or not. But I would think they would have 4 options to choose from for caste attributes with 2 available slots and can choose any non-caste attribute as a favored attribute with 2 slots. I don't know if casteless is still a thing. If thats the case I would give the casteless 2 caste attributes and one favored witht he rotating caste anima power. <br /> <br /> Adding in hearts-blood shape changing &quot;knacks&quot; it would give them a much more fluid/changing feel overall as an exalt type. <br /> <br /> Am I taking crazy pills?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T11:35:29-07:00","id":935711,"title":"","content":"I think Casteless might be a thing, but won't have any caste powers at all. But they definitely won't turn into chimera.<br /> <br /> Honestly, if Lunars with Castes have 2 caste and 2 favoured, there's no reason not to say Casteless have 4 favoured. Then, when they get their caste, it's the one that fits (for example, if they have Strength, Dex, Charisma and Intelligence, they become a Full Moon).<br /> Otherwise you get the awkwardness where the XP cost for buying stuff becomes cheaper part-way through the game when playing a Casteless Lunar, once you get your caste, which encourages you to not spend XP until you get a caste, which is kind of weird, but more importantly, unnecessary.<br /> <br /> Anyway. I can see the caste powers per caste attribute being interesting. I don't think it'll happen, because the devs seem keen on pushing the idea of Castes as more important than before, and more defined. But then, Lunars are very different from Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T12:15:44-07:00","id":935735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/932934-lunar-castes-have-always-been-a-bit-different?p=935711#post935711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Casteless might be a thing, but won't have any caste powers at all. But they definitely won't turn into chimera.<br /> Anyway. I can see the caste powers per caste attribute being interesting. I don't think it'll happen, because the devs seem keen on pushing the idea of Castes as more important than before, and more defined. But then, Lunars are very different from Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a place in which Devs talk about this sort of thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T11:47:03-07:00","id":936173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maudova</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/932934-lunar-castes-have-always-been-a-bit-different?p=934870#post934870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoops wasn't intentional.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry. I meant that that I wanted to respond to you, but that doing so in that thread would have derailed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T08:33:49-07:00","id":937106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/932934-lunar-castes-have-always-been-a-bit-different?p=936173#post936173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=